(** * Ed25519 Edwards scalarmult — bedrock2 implementation (PENDING).
 *
 * Discharge target for [Scalarmult.v]'s 2 [Parameter]s + 2 [Axiom]s.
 * Kept as `.v.todo` so dune skips it until ready to build.
 *
 * ============================================================
 * PREREQUISITE CHAIN (discovered 2026-04-26)
 * ============================================================
 *
 * Closing Phase 1.3 has FIVE serial dependencies, not the two
 * originally identified. From bottom to top:
 *
 *   0. **Make `fiat-crypto/.../X25519/EdwardsXYZT.v` build in AUCurves'
 *      dune setup.** That file currently does NOT compile in our
 *      project (no `EdwardsXYZT.vo` in `_build`). It imports
 *      `compiler.MMIO`, `compiler.Pipeline`, `compiler.Symbols` —
 *      bedrock2 compiler-stack libraries that aren't in our dune
 *      `theories` list. Investigation needed: are these imports
 *      actually used in the file's content, or just leftover from
 *      a CompCert-style end-to-end demonstration? If unused: strip
 *      and rebuild. If used: add the `compiler` theory to AUCurves'
 *      dune theories, OR write a slimmed-down version of the file
 *      that doesn't depend on them. ~half-day investigation + fix.
 *
 *   1. **64-bit port of `EdwardsXYZT.v` atoms.** The fiat-crypto
 *      version is bound to FE310CSemantics + Bitwidth32 (RISC-V
 *      32-bit). Ed25519 needs Bitwidth64 + BasicC64Semantics. The
 *      `Definition func`s should mostly be width-agnostic syntax
 *      trees, but the `Local Notation` for field offsets uses
 *      `felem_size` which depends on the field representation
 *      (UnsaturatedSolinas at 64-bit gives the same 40-byte felem
 *      as 32-bit, so notations may transfer). The proofs
 *      ([add_precomputed_ok] at line 504 etc.) are ~90s `repeat
 *      single_step` per the comment in the file — should mostly
 *      port automatically if the helper Ltac (`split_stack_at_n_in`,
 *      `solve_mem`, `single_step` etc.) ports. ~150 LoC bedrock2 +
 *      ~200 LoC re-proofs + ~100 LoC helper Ltac copy = ~450 LoC
 *      file. 1-3 days focused work.
 *
 *   2. **`ed25519_scalarmult_base` bedrock2 body + WP proof.** The
 *      sketch below assumes the 64-bit atoms exist and are callable.
 *      ~150-300 LoC bedrock2 + ~300-700 LoC WP proof.
 *
 *   3. **`ed25519_sign` body** (Sign.v). ~300 LoC + ~200 LoC WP.
 *
 *   4. **`ed25519_verify` body** (Verify.v). ~150 LoC + ~150 LoC WP.
 *
 * Total realistic Phase 1.3-1.5 closure cost: 4-5 weeks focused
 * effort, mostly serial. The first prerequisite (#0) is potentially
 * the cheapest unblocker but its size depends on what those
 * compiler.* imports are actually doing.
 *
 * ============================================================
 * CONCRETE BEDROCK2 SKETCH (paste-and-adapt for next session)
 * ============================================================
 *
 * Imports needed:
 *
 *   From Stdlib Require Import String List ZArith.
 *   Require Import bedrock2.Syntax bedrock2.NotationsCustomEntry.
 *   Require Import bedrock2.WeakestPrecondition bedrock2.ProgramLogic.
 *   Require Import bedrock2.Map.Separation bedrock2.Map.SeparationLogic.
 *   Require Import bedrock2.BasicC64Semantics.
 *   Require Import coqutil.Macros.WithBaseName.
 *   Require Import Crypto.Bedrock.End2End.X25519.EdwardsXYZT.
 *   Require Import Crypto.Bedrock.End2End.X25519.Field25519.
 *   Require Import Crypto.Spec.Curve25519.
 *   Require Import Crypto.Spec.CompleteEdwardsCurve.
 *   Require Import Bedrock.End2End.Ed25519.Scalarmult.
 *
 * Layout (mirrors EdwardsXYZT.v): a projective point is 5 felems
 * × 40 bytes = 200 bytes total, fields (X, Y, Z, Ta, Tb).
 * Local notations for field offsets are in EdwardsXYZT.v lines 60-64.
 *
 * Helper functions needed (NOT YET IN TREE):
 *
 *   1. fe25519_select_znz: bedrock2 cmov for one felem.
 *      Signature: func! (out, src_if_zero, src_if_nonzero, sel).
 *      Definition would mirror Field25519.v's existing select_znz
 *      synthesis (use unsaturated_solinas_ops's selectznz_op).
 *      ~10 LoC.
 *
 *   2. cmov_5felems: bedrock2 cmov over a 5-felem (200-byte) point.
 *      Wraps fe25519_select_znz 5x for X, Y, Z, Ta, Tb.
 *      ~12 LoC bedrock2.
 *
 *   3. fe25519_from_word_at: write a single u64 into the i-th felem.
 *      Already exists in Field25519.v as fe25519_from_word.
 *
 * Constants needed (NOT YET IN TREE):
 *
 *   4. B_precomputed: a Definition of Curve25519.E.B in
 *      precomputed_point form (half_ypx, half_ymx, xyd as 3 felems).
 *      Compute via vm_compute from B's affine coords (in Spec/Curve25519.v
 *      indirectly via E.B). ~20 LoC including the vm_compute proof.
 *      Actual byte sequence: known constant, but compute via Coq for
 *      audit-correctness rather than hardcoding.
 *
 * Bedrock2 function — ed25519_scalarmult_base (constant-time):
 *
 *   Definition ed25519_scalarmult_base := func! (out, scalar) {
 *     stackalloc 200 as ACC;
 *     stackalloc 200 as TMP;
 *     fe25519_from_word(ACC, $0);              (* X = 0 *)
 *     fe25519_from_word(ACC + $40, $1);        (* Y = 1 *)
 *     fe25519_from_word(ACC + $80, $1);        (* Z = 1 *)
 *     fe25519_from_word(ACC + $120, $0);       (* Ta = 0 *)
 *     fe25519_from_word(ACC + $160, $0);       (* Tb = 0 *)
 *     i = $255;
 *     while ($0 <= i) {
 *       double(ACC, ACC);
 *       byte = load1(scalar + (i >> $3));
 *       bit = (byte >> (i & $7)) & $1;
 *       add_precomputed(TMP, ACC, B_precomputed);
 *       cmov_5felems(ACC, TMP, bit);
 *       i = i - $1
 *     };
 *     memmove(out, ACC, $200)
 *   }.
 *
 * The variable-time variant ed25519_scalarmult takes a point P:
 *
 *   Definition ed25519_scalarmult := func! (out, scalar, P) {
 *     stackalloc 200 as ACC;
 *     stackalloc 160 as P_cached;            (* cached form is 4 felems *)
 *     to_cached(P_cached, P, fe25519_d);     (* fe25519_d is the curve d *)
 *     (* init ACC to identity as above *)
 *     ...
 *     i = $255;
 *     while ($0 <= i) {
 *       double(ACC, ACC);
 *       byte = load1(scalar + (i >> $3));
 *       bit = (byte >> (i & $7)) & $1;
 *       if (bit) {
 *         readd(ACC, ACC, P_cached)
 *       };
 *       i = i - $1
 *     };
 *     memmove(out, ACC, $200)
 *   }.
 *
 * Spec — ed25519_scalarmult_base_correct (Hoare triple shape):
 *
 *   Theorem ed25519_scalarmult_base_correct :
 *     forall functions t m (out_ptr scalar_ptr : word)
 *            (out_init : list Byte.byte) (scalar : list Byte.byte)
 *            (R : Semantics.mem -> Prop),
 *       length out_init = 200%nat ->
 *       length scalar = 32%nat ->
 *       (out_init$@out_ptr * scalar$@scalar_ptr * R)%sep m ->
 *       map.get functions "ed25519_scalarmult_base" =
 *         Some ed25519_scalarmult_base ->
 *       WeakestPrecondition.call functions "ed25519_scalarmult_base" t m
 *         [out_ptr; scalar_ptr]
 *         (fun t' m' rets =>
 *            t' = t /\ rets = nil /\
 *            exists out_pt,
 *              (* out is a serialized projective point *)
 *              decode_proj_point out = Some out_pt /\
 *              (* and equals scalar · B as an affine point *)
 *              E.eq (Extended.to_affine out_pt)
 *                   (E.mul (decode_le_scalar scalar) Curve25519.E.B) /\
 *              (out$@out_ptr * scalar$@scalar_ptr * R)%sep m').
 *
 * WP proof structure:
 *
 *   straightline.  (* break out the stackalloc and 5 fe25519_from_word *)
 *   handle_call.   (* for each fe25519_from_word_correct *)
 *   ... (* establish ACC = identity in extended coords *)
 *
 *   apply Loops.tailrec  (* or while invariant lemma of choice *)
 *     with
 *       (loop_inv := fun i ACC_state =>
 *          ACC_state = (high (255-i) bits of scalar) · B);
 *
 *   intros.
 *   handle_call (double_ok).
 *   handle_call (add_precomputed_ok).
 *   handle_call (cmov_5felems_ok).  (* needs the new cmov primitive *)
 *
 *   (* close the invariant by case analysis on bit *)
 *
 *   straightline.
 *   handle_call (memmove_correct).
 *   ecancel_assumption.
 *
 * Estimate: ~150-300 LoC bedrock2 program text + helpers, ~300-700
 * LoC WP proof. Multi-day focused effort. The hardest part is the
 * loop invariant tying the bit-position bookkeeping to E.mul.
 *
 * Test plan after closure:
 *   - Print Assumptions on both _correct theorems
 *   - Expect "Closed under the global context"
 *   - KAT test: ed25519_scalarmult_base [1, 0, ..., 0] should equal B
 *
 * ============================================================
 * REASON THIS FILE IS NOT YET .v
 * ============================================================
 *
 * 1. Helper primitives (cmov_5felems, B_precomputed) need to be
 *    defined first. ~50 LoC.
 * 2. WP proof requires interactive iteration via MCP/CoqIDE; cannot
 *    be reliably written in batch.
 * 3. Multi-day focused work expected.
 *
 * When picking up: rename to .v, follow the sketch above, expect
 * 5-10 iterations on cmov_5felems and the loop invariant. Reference
 * EdwardsXYZT.v's add_precomputed_ok proof at line 504 for the WP
 * style to mimic.
 *)
